---
import { codexMarketplace, marketplace } from "@data/navigation";
import { providers } from "@data/providers";
---

<div class="doc-body page-wrap prose">
  <section>
    <h2>Install from npm</h2>
    <p>Use the provider matching your agent environment:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>npx vitaecontext install --provider codex</code></pre>
    <p>Replace <code>codex</code> with another supported value listed below.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Supported provider values</h2>
    <div class="simple-table" role="table" aria-label="Supported provider values">
      {providers.map((provider) => <div role="row"><strong role="cell">{provider.id}</strong><span role="cell">{provider.name}</span><code role="cell">{provider.globalTarget}</code></div>)}
    </div>
    <p><a href="/providers/">See provider-specific commands and invocation examples.</a></p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Claude Code marketplace</h2>
    <p>Claude Code also supports a plugin marketplace installation:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>{marketplace.addCommand}
{marketplace.installCommand}</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Codex plugin marketplace</h2>
    <p>A cloned product repository includes a native Codex plugin backed by the same canonical skills:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>{codexMarketplace.addCommand}
{codexMarketplace.installCommand}</code></pre>
    <p>Direct npm skill installation remains supported and does not require the plugin marketplace.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Local checkout</h2>
    <p>Maintainers can test an unpublished checkout from the product repository:</p>
    <pre class="code-block"><code>git clone https://github.com/vitaecontext/vitaecontext.git
cd vitaecontext
npx . install --provider codex</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Useful install flags</h2>
    <dl class="definition-list">
      <div><dt><code>--project-root &lt;dir&gt;</code></dt><dd>Install relative to a project instead of the global default.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>--target-dir &lt;dir&gt;</code></dt><dd>Use an exact skill destination. Required for the shared provider.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>--commands-target-dir &lt;dir&gt;</code></dt><dd>Override command-wrapper placement where supported.</dd></div>
      <div><dt><code>--force</code></dt><dd>Replace existing VitaeContext files without prompting.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <aside class="note"><strong>Career files are separate.</strong><p>Installing skills does not collect or upload career material. Provider data rules apply when a user later supplies files to that provider.</p></aside>
</div>
